  8 │ 
  9 │ Our February star party was an absolute success! Over 40 eager astronomers gathered at our observatory site to observe the night sky through various telescopes, learn from experienced guides, and share their passion for astronomy. The clear weather provided excellent visibility of the Milky Way, as well as several bright planets including Jupiter and Mars.
    · ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    ·                                                                                                                                                                                    ╰── Dms tell: dms.qwen
 10 │ 
    ╰────

dms.qwen

  ⚠ Dms tell: dms.qwen
    ╭─[corpus/llm/email/062a9d6f268e8994.md:11:1]
 10 │ 
 11 │ We had a special guest, Dr. Emily Starbright (pseudonym), who shared her expertise in deep-sky imaging. She guided us through the night sky using state-of-the-art equipment, making our star party even more engaging than ever before. The highlight of the evening was undoubtedly the view of Saturn and its rings, illuminated by a full moon. Participants were impressed not only with what they saw but also with how to capture such celestial beauty.
    · ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
